#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/testing/functional_testing.rst:3
msgid "Functional Testing"
msgstr "Functional Testing"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/testing/functional_testing.rst:5
msgid ""
"Functional tests test software the way a user would. They simulate a user "
"browsing the website, but they do these steps in an automated way. phpBB "
"allows you to write such tests. This document will tell you how."
msgstr ""
"Functional tests test software the way a user would. They simulate a user "
"browsing the website, but they do these steps in an automated way. phpBB "
"allows you to write such tests. This document will tell you how."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/testing/functional_testing.rst:10
msgid "Running Functional Tests"
msgstr "Running Functional Tests"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/testing/functional_testing.rst:12
msgid ""
"Information on how to run tests is available in the GitHub repository at "
"`<https://github.com/phpbb/phpbb/blob/3.2.x/tests/RUNNING_TESTS.md>`_. You "
"can switch the branch to check instructions for a specific version of phpBB."
msgstr ""
"Information on how to run tests is available in the GitHub repository at "
"`<https://github.com/phpbb/phpbb/blob/3.2.x/tests/RUNNING_TESTS.md>`_. You "
"can switch the branch to check instructions for a specific version of phpBB."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/testing/functional_testing.rst:17
msgid "Writing Functional Tests"
msgstr "Writing Functional Tests"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/testing/functional_testing.rst:19
msgid ""
"Your test case will have to inherit from the ``phpbb_functional_test_case`` "
"class. You will be able to make requests to a fresh phpBB installation. "
"Also, be sure to put the file into the ``tests/functional/`` folder and to "
"add the ``@group functional`` doc block above the class, so the tests are "
"correctly executed."
msgstr ""
"Your test case will have to inherit from the ``phpbb_functional_test_case`` "
"class. You will be able to make requests to a fresh phpBB installation. "
"Also, be sure to put the file into the ``tests/functional/`` folder and to "
"add the ``@group functional`` doc block above the class, so the tests are "
"correctly executed."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/testing/functional_testing.rst:47
msgid ""
"There is a ``bootstrap()`` method where you can put code that is run before "
"the test. Here you can set up some objects after the installation that are "
"required for your test. Then you can define your tests, just as you would "
"normally, by prefixing methods with ``test_``. In this case we will be "
"testing the index."
msgstr ""
"There is a ``bootstrap()`` method where you can put code that is run before "
"the test. Here you can set up some objects after the installation that are "
"required for your test. Then you can define your tests, just as you would "
"normally, by prefixing methods with ``test_``. In this case we will be "
"testing the index."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/testing/functional_testing.rst:53
msgid "Goutte and Assertions"
msgstr "Goutte and Assertions"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/testing/functional_testing.rst:55
msgid ""
"The functional testing framework is built using `Goutte <https://github.com/"
"fabpot/Goutte>`_, which makes HTTP requests and allows us to interact with "
"the page. The Goutte \"client\" is available in your tests through ``$this-"
">request($method, $path)``. Alternatively you can also access it directly "
"through ``$this->client``."
msgstr ""
"The functional testing framework is built using `Goutte <https://github.com/"
"fabpot/Goutte>`_, which makes HTTP requests and allows us to interact with "
"the page. The Goutte \"client\" is available in your tests through ``$this-"
">request($method, $path)``. Alternatively you can also access it directly "
"through ``$this->client``."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/testing/functional_testing.rst:61
msgid ""
"When calling ``request()``, you will get a crawler, which allows you to "
"fetch parts of the page using CSS selectors. Here is an example:"
msgstr ""
"When calling ``request()``, you will get a crawler, which allows you to "
"fetch parts of the page using CSS selectors. Here is an example:"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/testing/functional_testing.rst:82
msgid ""
"We perform a GET request to ``index.php``, then apply a CSS filter, querying "
"for the .topiclist class. Then we make sure our query matched something."
msgstr ""
"We perform a GET request to ``index.php``, then apply a CSS filter, querying "
"for the .topiclist class. Then we make sure our query matched something."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/testing/functional_testing.rst:85
msgid ""
"If the board's index page were broken, our test would catch this, allowing "
"us to detect the issue and fix it. The more things you test, the more "
"breakages you will catch early."
msgstr ""
"If the board's index page were broken, our test would catch this, allowing "
"us to detect the issue and fix it. The more things you test, the more "
"breakages you will catch early."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/testing/functional_testing.rst:89
msgid ""
"For more information what you can do with Goutte, check out the `GitHub "
"project <https://github.com/fabpot/Goutte>`_, `Ryan Weaver's Goutte tutorial "
"<http://www.phparch.com/2010/04/four-new-php-5-3-components-and-goutte-a-"
"simple-web-scraper/>`_ and `Symfony's testing documentation <http://symfony."
"com/doc/2.0/book/testing.html#the-test-client>`_."
msgstr ""
"For more information what you can do with Goutte, check out the `GitHub "
"project <https://github.com/fabpot/Goutte>`_, `Ryan Weaver's Goutte tutorial "
"<http://www.phparch.com/2010/04/four-new-php-5-3-components-and-goutte-a-"
"simple-web-scraper/>`_ and `Symfony's testing documentation <http://symfony."
"com/doc/2.0/book/testing.html#the-test-client>`_."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/testing/functional_testing.rst:95
msgid "Authentication"
msgstr "Authentication"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/testing/functional_testing.rst:97
msgid ""
"Many functional tests will require the user to be logged in. To do so, you "
"can use the ``login()`` method inherited from the "
"``phpbb_functional_test_case`` class. This method will assign the user's SID "
"to the inherited class property ``$this->sid``. You will need to append this "
"to the URLs that the logged-in user will be navigating to in order to hold "
"the session. For usage examples, view the logout test in `tests/functional/"
"auth_test.php <https://github.com/phpbb/phpbb/blob/3.2.x/tests/functional/"
"auth_test.php>`_."
msgstr ""
"Many functional tests will require the user to be logged in. To do so, you "
"can use the ``login()`` method inherited from the "
"``phpbb_functional_test_case`` class. This method will assign the user's SID "
"to the inherited class property ``$this->sid``. You will need to append this "
"to the URLs that the logged-in user will be navigating to in order to hold "
"the session. For usage examples, view the logout test in `tests/functional/"
"auth_test.php <https://github.com/phpbb/phpbb/blob/3.2.x/tests/functional/"
"auth_test.php>`_."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/testing/functional_testing.rst:106
msgid "Localisation"
msgstr "Localisation"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/testing/functional_testing.rst:108
msgid ""
"In tests, as in phpBB itself, do not use hard-coded language unless "
"absolutely necessary. Instead, use the ``$this->add_lang()`` and ``$this-"
">lang()`` methods. Both act very similarly to their counterparts in the "
"``\\phpbb\\user`` class. Note that ``language/en/common.php`` is "
"automatically loaded by the test framework."
msgstr ""
"In tests, as in phpBB itself, do not use hard-coded language unless "
"absolutely necessary. Instead, use the ``$this->add_lang()`` and ``$this-"
">lang()`` methods. Both act very similarly to their counterparts in the "
"``\\phpbb\\user`` class. Note that ``language/en/common.php`` is "
"automatically loaded by the test framework."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/testing/functional_testing.rst:131
msgid ""
"For more usage examples, please view `tests/functional/lang_test.php "
"<https://github.com/phpbb/phpbb/blob/3.2.x/tests/functional/lang_test.php>`_."
msgstr ""
"For more usage examples, please view `tests/functional/lang_test.php "
"<https://github.com/phpbb/phpbb/blob/3.2.x/tests/functional/lang_test.php>`_."
